IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc12-logic.l4 -- helpers for part ccc12 (Criminal Code (Canada), Part IX, ss 321 to 378). Not a provision of the Code.
-- DEPARTURE FROM THE BRIEF'S NAMING FORM (recorded in NOTES.md, Seams): these names begin `ccc12 ` and not with a section label,
-- because they implement no section; the prefix cannot collide with any other part's names.
--
-- Three-valued logic over MAYBE BOOLEAN. JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are definite answers; NOTHING is "the text does not answer".
--   `ccc12 and`: a JUST FALSE limb makes the conjunction JUST FALSE (a definite "no" settles it); otherwise a NOTHING limb gives NOTHING.
--   `ccc12 or`:  a JUST TRUE limb makes the disjunction JUST TRUE; otherwise a NOTHING limb gives NOTHING.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE: nothing here does.

§ `Three-valued logic`

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ccc12 and` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST x THEN IF x
                     THEN b
                     ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN CONSIDER b
                      WHEN JUST y THEN IF y THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST FALSE
                      WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN, b IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ccc12 or` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST x THEN IF x
                     THEN JUST TRUE
                     ELSE b
    WHEN NOTHING THEN CONSIDER b
                      WHEN JUST y THEN IF y THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
                      WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

GIVEN a IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ccc12 not` MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN JUST x THEN JUST (NOT x)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- `ccc12 holds` lifts a plain yes/no the person states into the three-valued answer.
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ccc12 holds` MEANS JUST a

§ `Punishment limbs`

-- A limb of a penalty provision "guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than N" is a Punishment
-- (core record) whose mode is `by indictment`, whose maximum imprisonment is the stated term, and whose other fields say none is stated.
GIVEN `the maximum imprisonment` IS AN Imprisonment
GIVETH A Punishment
`ccc12 an indictable limb` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
        `mode` IS `by indictment`
        `maximum imprisonment` IS `the maximum imprisonment`
        `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
        `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
        `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

GIVEN `the maximum imprisonment` IS AN Imprisonment
      `the minimum imprisonment` IS AN Imprisonment
GIVETH A Punishment
`ccc12 an indictable limb with a minimum` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
        `mode` IS `by indictment`
        `maximum imprisonment` IS `the maximum imprisonment`
        `minimum imprisonment` IS `the minimum imprisonment`
        `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
        `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

-- A limb "guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than N" with the
-- term stated by the section (as opposed to the general penalty of s 787(1), which the sections that state none take as an input).
GIVEN `the maximum imprisonment` IS AN Imprisonment
GIVETH A Punishment
`ccc12 a summary limb` MEANS
    Punishment WITH
        `mode` IS `on summary conviction`
        `maximum imprisonment` IS `the maximum imprisonment`
        `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
        `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
        `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`

-- The same, where the punishment function itself answers NOTHING.
GIVEN limbs IS A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
GIVETH A MAYBE `Class of offence`
`ccc12 the class of the offence from its possible limbs` MEANS
    CONSIDER limbs
    WHEN JUST ls THEN `ccc12 the class of the offence from its limbs` ls
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the section's punishment function did not answer

-- The class of the offence, worked out from the limbs a penalty provision states: both modes is "both indictable and punishable on
-- summary conviction", one mode is that mode, no limb is NOTHING.
GIVEN limbs IS A LIST OF Punishment
GIVETH A MAYBE `Class of offence`
`ccc12 the class of the offence from its limbs` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `an indictable limb` AND `a summary limb`
        THEN JUST `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`
        IF `an indictable limb`
        THEN JUST `an indictable offence`
        IF `a summary limb`
        THEN JUST `an offence punishable on summary conviction`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the provision states no limb
    WHERE
        `an indictable limb` MEANS any (`is by indictment`) limbs
        `a summary limb` MEANS any (`is on summary conviction`) limbs
        `is by indictment` p MEANS p's `mode` EQUALS `by indictment`
        `is on summary conviction` p MEANS p's `mode` EQUALS `on summary conviction`
